  "id": "COMPOUND:43707 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Alpinone 3-acetate is shown to have a direct target of MIP, which is a known target of HepG2 cells. This relationship is supported by multiple evidence paths, all of which indicate that Alpinone 3-acetate interacts with MIP and subsequently affects HepG2. The mechanism involves MIP being a target of Alpinone 3-acetate, and the downstream effect on HepG2 is consistent across different molecular structures of MIP, suggesting that the interaction is not specific to a single isomer. The presence of multiple MIP isomers with similar target effects further supports the notion that Alpinone 3-acetate acts through a common pathway on MIP, which in turn influences HepG2. The evidence suggests a direct, mechanistic link between Alpinone 3-acetate and HepG2, with MIP serving as a critical mediator in this relationship.",
